public class MaximumNumber {

	public static void main(String[] args) {

		int a=10, b=20, c=25,max;
		max = (a>b)?(a>c?a:c):(b>c?b:c);
		System.out.println("Maximum number among " +a+ ", " +b+ " and " +c+ " is "  + max);

	}

}


OUTPUT:

Maximum number among 10, 20 and 25 is 25

DESCRIPTION:

The ternary operator checks if a > b. If true, it then compares a with c, otherwise, it compares b with c.
The maximum value is assigned to the variable max, which is then printed.
